# Payagent — Backend Rules (Spring Boot 3.3 + Java 21)

**Source of truth:** `AGENTS.md` §1, §2, §3, §4, §5. This file adds backend-specific guidance.

## Package Ownership
```
com.payagent.common.contracts/   → Member A (canonical DTOs/Enums)
com.payagent.auth/               → Member A (JWT, login, deal guard)
com.payagent.deals/              → Member A (deal lifecycle, offers)
com.payagent.mandates/           → Member A (versioned mandates, UtilityCalculator)
com.payagent.agreements/         → Member A (AgreementService, RFC-8785 hash)
com.payagent.paypal/             → Member B (OAuth, Invoicing v2, Orders v2, Webhooks)
com.payagent.settlement/         → Member B (dual-rail settlement flow)
com.payagent.ai/                 → Member C (IntakeExtractor, NegotiationAgent, PromptSanitizer)
com.payagent.evidence/           → Member E (SHA-256 storage, signed URLs)
com.payagent.disputes/           → Member E (dispute freeze, resolution)
com.payagent.realtime/           → Member E (WebSocket STOMP, cursor replay)
com.payagent.config/             → Member A/E (SecurityConfig, PayPalEnvironmentGuard)
com.payagent.web/                → Member A (HealthController, future REST controllers)
```

## Required Patterns

### 1. REST Controllers
- Base path: `/api/v1`
- Mutating endpoints: require `Idempotency-Key` header
- Return canonical DTOs from `com.payagent.common.contracts`
- Validate request bodies with `@Valid` + Jakarta validation annotations on records
- Never expose counterparty's `MandateDTO` in responses

### 2. Security
- `SecurityConfig`: stateless, JWT-ready, permits `/actuator/health/**`, `/api/v1/health`
- JWT filter/token provider: Member A implements in `auth/`
- Object-level authorization: check deal membership + role in service layer

### 3. Database & Flyway
- Schema: `V1__init.sql` (Member A owns evolution)
- JPA: `ddl-auto: validate` — Flyway manages schema
- Test profile (`application-test.yml`): excludes DataSource/JPA/Flyway auto-config

### 4. PayPal Integration (Member B Only)
- `PayPalEnvironmentGuard` fails fast if base URL ≠ sandbox
- OAuth token cache with TTL
- Invoicing v2: `POST /v2/invoicing/invoices` (detail.note = termsHashSha256), `/send`, `/payments`, `/cancel`
- Orders v2: `intent: AUTHORIZE`, `/authorize`, `/capture`, `/void`
- Webhooks: verify signature via `POST /v1/notifications/verify-webhook-signature`, deduplicate `event_id` in `paypal_events`

### 5. AI Integration (Member C Only)
- Spring AI ChatClient via OpenAI-compatible starter
- `extractDealIntake(rawText)` → `StructuredTermsDTO` (validated by Member A's MandateService)
- `draftBoundedCounterOffer(context, mandate, offer)` → `ProposedOfferDTO`
- Counterparty text wrapped in `<untrusted_counterparty_data>...</untrusted_counterparty_data>`
- Deterministic fallback on LLM timeout (>6s) or schema violation
- Benchmark: 20 prompts, 100% JSON schema validity, p95 < 5s

### 6. Evidence & Realtime (Member E Only)
- Evidence: MIME allowlist (.zip/.pdf/.png), max 10MB, streaming SHA-256, storage outside web root, 15-min HMAC-signed download URLs
- Disputes: `POST /api/v1/deals/{id}/disputes` → `DealStatus=DISPUTED`, blocks capture
- WebSocket: `/ws/deals/{id}` with JWT header + `?afterSeq=` replay, masks counterparty mandate fields

## Testing
- Unit tests: JUnit 5 + MockMvc (`@WebMvcTest`, `@ActiveProfiles("test")`)
- Contract tests: `ContractFixtureDeserializationTest`, `ContractTypeScriptParityTest`
- Integration tests: require Docker (Postgres) or testcontainers
- Release gates (Member F): TST-01..TST-15 in `releasegates/` package

## Commands (from `services/api/`)
```bash
./mvnw -B test                    # All tests (H2 profile for unit)
./mvnw -B -DskipTests package     # Package JAR
./mvnw -B test -Dtest=HealthControllerTest
./mvnw -B test -Dtest=ContractTypeScriptParityTest
```

## Do Not
- Add dependencies without coordinating (esp. Spring AI version compatibility)
- Hard-code PayPal URLs or credentials
- Return `MandateDTO` for counterparty in any endpoint
- Use floating-point for money
- Skip idempotency keys on mutating endpoints
- Disable `PayPalEnvironmentGuard`